      "title": "No, not, none",
      "canDo": "Deny, contrast, and correct simple information",
      "tip": {
        "title": "Use nicht for actions and kein for nouns",
        "body": "Use **nicht** to negate an action or description: **Ich arbeite nicht** and **Das ist nicht richtig**. English usually uses “not” with an auxiliary verb, but German can place **nicht** later in the clause.\n\nForms of **kein** change for gender, number, and case. In the nominative, use **kein** with masculine and neuter nouns and **keine** with feminine and plural nouns: **Das ist kein Kaffee** and **Das ist keine Milch**. In the accusative, neuter **kein Wasser** and feminine **keine Milch** stay the same, while a masculine noun takes **keinen**, as in **Ich trinke keinen Kaffee**. These forms express English “not a,” “not any,” or “no.”",
        "examples": [
          { "target": "Ich arbeite heute nicht.", "source": "I am not working today." },
          { "target": "Das ist kein Kaffee.", "source": "That is not coffee." },
          { "target": "Ich trinke keine Milch.", "source": "I do not drink milk." }
        ]
      },
